### 18.5 Team Management

#### 18.5.1 Get Team Members
**Endpoint**: `GET /api/v1/settings/team/members`

**Query Parameters** (optional):
- `page`: number (default: 1)
- `limit`: number (default: 50)
- `search`: string (optional, search by name or email)

**Response**:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "members": [
      {
        "id": "string",
        "name": "string",
        "email": "string",
        "role": "string",
        "avatar": "string | null",
        "status": "active" | "pending" | "inactive",
        "invitedAt": "ISO 8601 datetime",
        "joinedAt": "ISO 8601 datetime | null",
        "lastActiveAt": "ISO 8601 datetime | null"
      }
    ],
    "pagination": {
      "page": number,
      "limit": number,
      "total": number,
      "totalPages": number
    }
  }
}
```

#### 18.5.2 Invite Team Members
**Endpoint**: `POST /api/v1/settings/team/invite`

**Request Body**:
```json
{
  "invites": [
    {
      "email": "string",
      "role": "string"
    }
  ]
}
```

**Validation Rules**:
- `invites`: Array, minimum 1 item
- Each invite must have:
  - `email`: Required, valid email format, must not already be a team member
  - `role`: Required, must be one of: "Admin", "Editor", "Read-only"

**Response**:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "invited": [
      {
        "email": "string",
        "role": "string",
        "inviteToken": "string",
        "expiresAt": "ISO 8601 datetime"
      }
    ],
    "failed": [
      {
        "email": "string",
        "reason": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "message": "Invitations sent successfully"
}
```

#### 18.5.3 Update Team Member Role
**Endpoint**: `PUT /api/v1/settings/team/members/{memberId}/role`

**Path Parameters**:
- `memberId`: string (required)

**Request Body**:
```json
{
  "role": "string"
}
```

**Response**:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "id": "string",
    "role": "string",
    "updatedAt": "ISO 8601 datetime"
  },
  "message": "Team member role updated successfully"
}
```

#### 18.5.4 Remove Team Member
**Endpoint**: `DELETE /api/v1/settings/team/members/{memberId}`

**Path Parameters**:
- `memberId`: string (required)

**Response**:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Team member removed successfully"
}
```

**Note**: Users should not be able to remove themselves from the team.

